[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I am  interested  in the implementation of  <strong>continued fractions</strong> in Mathlib, and in particular, their computations and the use of their coefficients.</p>\n<p>However, I noticed that  the already  existing version of  computable <code>GenContFract</code> only  works  for <code>FloorRing</code> and not <code>EuclideanDomain</code>.</p>\n<p>Moreover, the way <code>GenContFract.of</code> is implemented casts the value of the coefficients directly to <code>K</code>, which results in a  loss  of information about the correct type of the coefficients.</p>\n<p>As an alternative to this approach, I developed an implementation of continued fractions using the Euclidean algorithm.<br>\nI redefine an <code>EuclContFract</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The integer part `a₀` of the continued fraction. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The list of partial quotients `[a₁, a₂, …]`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(This could simply be a list,  but in this way it is closer to the already existing Mathlib version for <code>GenContFract</code>).</p>\n<p>Then, via the Euclidean <strong>algorithm</strong>, one produces:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">euclidSeq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanDomain</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">r_wellFounded</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fix</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanDomain</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">remainder_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and finally:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFrac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">euclidSeq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The continued fraction expansion of `k : K`, using a chosen numerator and denominator. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ofFrac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The continued fraction expansion of a rational number. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of_Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFrac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>together  with a proof of their correctness:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of_Q_eq_q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">convergents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">of_Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">of_Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">of_Q</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">num_div_den</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ofFrac_eq_convergent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact_mod_cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den_ne_zero</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of_eq_k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">convergents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ofFrac_eq_convergent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk'_num_den'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>My definitions are still compatible with the existing Mathlib version and I also provide some API to prove it, e.g.:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toGenContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GenContFract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GenContFract</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If you think this is valuable to Mathlib, I would be very happy to PR it.</p>\n<p>I would  also be very happy to hear any design comments or suggestions , and to share my code in general if it can be useful to someone</p>",
        "id": 602463340,
        "sender_full_name": "Nicola Falciola",
        "timestamp": 1781258558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't see how your approach applies to the real numbers, for instance. Can you comment on that?</p>",
        "id": 602478662,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1781262061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed this method does not apply to the real numbers. However with this method you can compute continued fraction of  <code>\\Q (i)</code>  (up to build a model of it with  <code>DecidebleEq</code>) and other number fields or function field rings while the other method basically only apply to the real numbers.</p>",
        "id": 602496978,
        "sender_full_name": "Nicola Falciola",
        "timestamp": 1781266114
    }
]